# Unit Tests

When adding or changing a **feature** (controllers, routes, services, models, utilities), **add or update unit tests in the same change**. Do not ship feature-only code without tests.

## Scope

- **New endpoints or handlers** — success, validation errors, not-found, and server/DB failures (mocked).
- **New business logic** — happy path, edge cases, and thrown/handled errors.
- **Bug fixes** — a regression test that fails without the fix.

## Conventions

- Place tests next to source (`*.test.ts`) or under `src/**/__tests__/`.
- Mock MongoDB, Express `req`/`res`, and external I/O; do not hit a real database in unit tests.
- Follow project standards: use `Logger` in production code under test paths only as needed; no `console.*` in `src/`.

## Before finishing

- Tests exist for the new behavior.
- Run the project test script (e.g. `npm test`) when available; if no runner is configured yet, add one (Vitest or Jest) and a `test` script in `package.json` as part of the feature work.

```typescript
// Example: controller test (pattern)
describe("createEmployee", () => {
  it("returns 201 when employee is created", async () => { /* ... */ });
  it("returns 409 on duplicate email", async () => { /* ... */ });
  it("returns 500 when create throws", async () => { /* ... */ });
});
```
